{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["To judge the people — even if Yitro came before the giving of the Torah, they had civil laws from of old, even though our Rabbis said that at Marah He gave them laws, as it is written there: שם שם לו חק ומשפט. And it appears that he came after the giving of the Torah. It is written here: אשר הוא חנה שם הר האלהים, and earlier it says: בחדש השלישי לצאת בני ישראל מארץ מצרים ביום הזה באו מדבר סיני, and ויסעו מרפידים ויבאו מדבר סיני ויחן שם ישראל נגד ההר. Thus the section of Rephidim and the encampment at the mountain preceded this section, and in order not to interrupt the sections of commandments, he anticipated the section of Yitro." "From the morning until the evening — because he alone judged the entire people and he had no assistants."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The lemma quotes שם twice; translated exactly as the Hebrew reads, though the first שם ('there') may be a dittography or the verse citation may be slightly corrupted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:59.493782063Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}